				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					37.56
				</span></i>
			: with Advs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκανῶς πεφυκότες</span>
			<i>of</i> good <i>natural ability,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				2.1.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσκόλως πεφ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					9.6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὕτως πεφ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					7.1.7
				</span></i>
			; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ καλῶς πεφυκότες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					989
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				2.20
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ βέλτιστα φύντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					431c
				</span></i>
			: then, simply, <i>to be</i> so and so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῦναι Ζηνὶ πιστὸν ἄγγελον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					969
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοῦ μήτηρ ἔφυς</span>”
